{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:22:13.674Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1769"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1769: the extension test harness accepts universal output controls on non-read commands that the native CLI refuses before dispatch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1769 (filed 2026-11-22, reproduced on 2026.11.22). createExtensionTestHarness().runCommand and runRegisteredCommandForTest accept universal output controls (outputBudget, outputLimit, outputInclude, outputCursor, and the other canonical read-output keys) on an extension command that declares no read_output. The native CLI refuses the same invocation before dispatch: pm probe echo --output-budget 1 --json exits 2 with \"Universal output controls apply only to read commands; probe echo is not a read surface.\" The native guard is validateReadOutputOptions (src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts), called in the CLI preAction hook (src/cli/main.ts) and in PmClient.run dispatchAction (src/sdk/runtime.ts) with the active extension registrations published. The harness (src/sdk/testing.ts runRegisteredCommandForTest) never calls it, so a package test passes for an invocation every real agent sees refused. This is the parity gap GH-1729 (pm-gh1729, closed) set out to close for read-output results; it did not cover pre-dispatch admission of the controls themselves. Duplicate check: searched \"extension test harness universal output controls read surface\"; pm-gh1729 and pm-extension-read-output-controls are closed and own result admission and the read_output opt-in, nothing owns the pre-dispatch control refusal in the harness."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["extensions","gh:1769","read-output","sdk","testing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:22:13.674Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:22:13.674Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A harness call to a non-read extension command with any universal output control fails with the native refusal's exit code and message; A command that declares read_output keeps accepting the controls, and malformed control values are refused as natively; A parity spec runs the same invocation through the harness and the built CLI and compares the refusals"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"runCommand refuses universal output controls on a non-read extension command with the same code, exit and message as native dispatch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1729","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-23T08:22:13.674Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"1e4eba82d1691544fe4b090d85f68855233b723c464d48fea44e2e6dc802ec83","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context"