{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T10:55:39.665Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-5mstyv","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T10:55:39.664Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 on PR #1772 (Codex and CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). Harness admission now also sees option keys spelled as flags: '--add-json' and 'add-json' fold to addJson (a notes mutation option, so outputLimit beside it refuses read_output_mutation_conflict as natively), and '--output-limit' folds to outputLimit (refused on a non-read command). Folding uses resolveExtensionFlagOptionKey and only adds the folded key, so required-flag and value validation still run afterwards in normalization. harness-parity.spec.ts covers both spellings and an unfoldable short key.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T10:55:39.665Z"}],"before_hash":"8718e91a82520a343039e9118089031e2b393ac79f981b81b56bb0df6d7332f6","after_hash":"fd1d4799d58bb3d9d4ffa7860d916785bc67380da83db8de7939ae8502feccae","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8575b06a267282b1914dd5ddcd8e27e72a3e5cfefceb728c8df11f084c25e8ac"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T11:57:25.824Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T11:57:25.823Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 on PR #1772 (Codex pass 3 and CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). (1) Codex P2: dashed output controls were folded for admission only, so options { '--output-budget': '400' } on a read command was formatted without the budget; the folded canonical controls now also reach native formatOutput, so it refuses output_budget_exceeded like outputBudget does. (2) CodeRabbit: a declared short alias of a mutation flag (-J for --add-json on notes) was not folded for admission; folding now maps a key equal to a declared short spelling to its handler key. (3) CodeRabbit: docs now state that the refusal covers the output-shaping controls and that a renderer-only --output-format stays accepted (hasCanonicalReadOutputOptions excludes it). harness-parity.spec.ts covers (1) and (2).\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T11:57:25.824Z"}],"before_hash":"fd1d4799d58bb3d9d4ffa7860d916785bc67380da83db8de7939ae8502feccae","after_hash":"90a18ae09769ffa65793e3a4190fed8437d1afbff21cd86eb8841ec3dee1bfe6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c3351cf7a3399041a2c8e2f707944eb4427bcc11e6f45333040320053ad4e141"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T12:46:05.984Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T12:46:05.983Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 4 on PR #1772 (Codex pass 4 and Greptile, 2026-11-23). (1) A declared short alias now folds with or without its dash (J as well as -J), as the option normalizer accepts both, so notes with J and outputLimit refuses read_output_mutation_conflict. (2) Output controls a caller passes through options now also reach the handler's context.global (global still wins), as a native --output-budget does, so a read handler that adapts to context.global.outputBudget behaves the same whichever way the harness receives it; formatting reads the same values. harness-parity.spec.ts covers both.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T12:46:05.984Z"}],"before_hash":"90a18ae09769ffa65793e3a4190fed8437d1afbff21cd86eb8841ec3dee1bfe6","after_hash":"b12ed6eb6d13abd11ff664c30eb2b3a58f7b0bfede667725877afa6e4138b739","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"918d39d7c9336bbd0c8f6fbb24fcaa65e8ae75ca4b46cd378eb3caf31e077dfb"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T13:39:46.629Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T13:39:46.628Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 5 on PR #1772 (CodeRabbit and Codex pass 5, 2026-11-23). Output controls forwarded from options to context.global: an explicit undefined in global no longer erases an admitted control (only defined global values override), a snake-case spelling such as output_limit is carried as outputLimit, an undefined canonical key no longer masks a dashed spelling during folding, and SDK-form values reach context.global in the string form native host flags deliver (a numeric limit as its decimal string, a selector list comma-joined). harness-parity.spec.ts covers each. The two remaining contrived gaps from the fifth Codex pass (an inactive duplicate inline field becoming effective, a negated mutation flag in harness admission) are filed as pm-2nwcgg.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T13:39:46.629Z"}],"before_hash":"b12ed6eb6d13abd11ff664c30eb2b3a58f7b0bfede667725877afa6e4138b739","after_hash":"204349d96ab91e057e7a115422e2be4cb266020c547fae78bbaa6bea4409d671","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"512b6f55a28764007c57eaf4db3d6c44f9a027b8554ecf4e1bde5a8d93af6155"}
